          "text": "Abdominal pain"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Patient reports intermittent crampy abdominal pain for 3–4 days, mainly around the umbilicus and left iliac fossa, described as like bad period pain. Severity 3–5/10. No clear food trigger or radiation. It does not wake her."
      }
    },
